dsh-github-triage 0.4.4

This package is an original implementation, licensed under MIT (see LICENSE).

Implementation ideas were studied from:
- deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness (MIT), official internal development skills
  commit e8f7b93: .agents/skills/dsh-client-ui-ux (including alignment, icons,
  spacing), dsh-responsive-ui and cordis-styling-nitpicking.
  https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/tree/e8f7b93/.agents/skills
  Applied relevant third-party Client UI, theme, responsive and ownership rules;
  host-workspace-only gates were not imported into this external bundle.
- w2112515/dsh-plugin-development (MIT), commit 4dab80c
  https://github.com/w2112515/dsh-plugin-development
  Studied authority/verification, component routing, installable-bundle,
  runtime-dynamic and workspace-plugin references and the read-only artifact
  checker. This package is an external installable bundle, not a DSH workspace
  package or a process-local dynamic plugin. No adapter was installed.
- bowenliang123/dsh-context 0.83.1 (commit 4d8fb8a) — Apache-2.0
  https://github.com/bowenliang123/dsh-context
  Studied sidebar/main slot pairing, connection Fetch routes, design tokens,
  overview cards, loading skeletons and on-demand detail lifetimes.
  For 0.4.1 also studied settings groups, stacked labels, min-width:0,
  container sizing and vertically resizable textareas.
- ItQianChen/dsh-github-flow — MIT
  https://github.com/ItQianChen/dsh-github-flow
  Studied gh credential reuse and repository review rule separation.
- PerryLink/dsh-github-bot — Apache-2.0
  https://github.com/PerryLink/dsh-github-bot
  Studied bounded read-only fetching, polling and PR-level evidence organization.

No source code snippets from these projects were transplanted, copied or
modified into this package. No upstream NOTICE content is incorporated.
Their licenses continue to apply to their respective original projects.

Runtime dependencies are distributed separately by npm:
- undici (MIT) — https://github.com/nodejs/undici
- zod (MIT) — https://github.com/colinhacks/zod
Their distributed packages retain their own copyright and license notices.

Official DeepSeek Harness rc.5 packages are host peers/development dependencies.
Local monorepo package conventions were followed under this repository's MIT license.


Browser bundle:
- zod 4.4.3 is bundled into lib/client.js for shared frontend/server validation.
  https://github.com/colinhacks/zod
  Its full MIT license follows.
- React, react/jsx-runtime, and @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-primitives are
  external host-shared modules, not redistributed inside this browser bundle.
- esbuild and jsdom are development/build/test tools only, not runtime assets.
- Browser registration/build conventions follow this monorepo's MIT-licensed
  dsh-draft-rescue and dsh-snip-attach and official DeepSeek Harness rc.5 (MIT).
  No official UI component implementation is copied; Modal is host-shared.
  The 0.4.1 repository form also uses host-shared Input and follows the
  rc.5 / rc.1 plugin install wizard's bounded Modal, scrolling body and
  persistent footer pattern, with DSH alias theme tokens.
  Version 0.4.3 uses host-shared Button, Input, Modal, Menu, SegmentedTabs,
  Pill, Tag, Checkbox and SettingsValueField; exports and used props were checked
  against local 0.2.1-rc.5 types/implementation and official dsh-v0.2.2-rc.1
  ui-primitives source. No UI component source or CSS is redistributed.
  The test-only harness reads exact component regions from the installed rc.5
  artifact into memory; CSS class maps replace CSS loading, not component logic.
